CON-12: report a cyclic treatment dependency as ERROR 161

getRemoval() set ErrCode = 1 when an equation reached a removal that was
still being evaluated, but treatmnt_treat() only reports the error, and skips
the apply pass, when ErrCode == ERR_CYCLIC_TREATMENT (161). The branch was
dead: the run went on with the cyclic removals set to 0 and no message. Set
ErrCode to ERR_CYCLIC_TREATMENT so the documented ERROR 161 is reported and
the run stops.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-12_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c b/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
index 3638cd3..66f414d 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
@@ -401,7 +401,7 @@ double  getRemoval(int p)
     // --- case where removal already being computed for another pollutant
     if ( R[p] > 1.0 || ErrCode )
     {
-        ErrCode = 1;
+        ErrCode = ERR_CYCLIC_TREATMENT;
         return 0.0;
     }
 
